            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Barely. The dominant failure mode is identical across manufacturers: belt-to-deck friction rises, the motor draws more current, and sustained draw destroys motors and boards. Lubricating every 40 to 50 hours addresses it on any machine — check the manual first, since some decks are pre-waxed and are ruined by silicone.",
          },
        },
      ],
    },
